      <item>
        <title>AlphaEvolve v4: evolutionary AI discovers 3 novel algorithms beating 50-year human records</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/alphaevolve-v4</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/alphaevolve-v4</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 15 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>AlphaEvolve v4 is DeepMind&#x27;s evolutionary code-discovery system. It evolves code (Python, C++, CUDA) via LLM-guided mutation + fitness evaluation, discovering novel algorithms that beat human-discovered records. v4 adds a multi-objective fitness landscape (speed + memory + accuracy) + a 10M-code-variant parallel evaluation farm. 3 novel algorithms discovered in 2026: (1) a matrix-multiplication algorithm beating Strassen&#x27;s 1969 record for 4×4 matrices (47 multiplications vs Strassen&#x27;s 49), (2) a sorting-network comparator count beating the 60-year record for 24-input networks (59 vs 60), (3) a fast-convolution CUDA kernel 2.3x faster than cuDNN&#x27;s optimised kernel for 3×3 conv on H100. All 3 algorithms are open-sourced under Apache 2.0 + verified by independent reproduction. The system runs on a 10,000-GPU evaluation farm; each evolution run tests ~2M code variants.</description>
        <category>CS - Evolutionary code discovery</category>
        <dc:creator>DeepMind AlphaEvolve team</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>NVIDIA Earth-2: 1km-resolution global climate digital twin at 1000x speedup</title>
        <link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-2-2026</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-2-2026</guid>
        <pubDate>Thu, 10 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>NVIDIA blog</source>
        <description>Earth-2 is NVIDIA&#x27;s climate digital twin — a 1km-resolution global atmosphere + ocean simulation running on 4,500 H100 GPUs. The 2026 update adds Modulus-NVIDIA physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) that achieve 1000x speedup over traditional WRF/MPAS climate models at equivalent resolution. Earth-2 can simulate 1 year of global climate in 3 hours (vs 4 months for WRF at 1km). The system has been validated against ERA5 reanalysis data: 0.94 correlation for 2m temperature, 0.91 for precipitation, 0.88 for 10m wind. Released as open-access via the Earth-2 cloud platform. 47 climate-research institutions have adopted it for IPCC AR7 contributions.</description>
        <category>Physics - Climate digital twin</category>
        <dc:creator>NVIDIA Earth-2 team + NOAA + ECMWF</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Gemini 2.5 medical: 1T-param multimodal model with native 3D medical imaging</title>
        <link>https://health.google/blog/gemini-25-medical</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://health.google/blog/gemini-25-medical</guid>
        <pubDate>Sat, 12 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Google Health blog</source>
        <description>Gemini 2.5 medical is a 1T-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts) multimodal LLM fine-tuned for clinical use. The 2026 medical update adds native 3D medical imaging support (CT, MRI volumes processed directly — no 2D slicing required) + a longitudinal patient-timeline understanding module. On the MultiMedQA-Pro benchmark (500 multi-turn clinical conversations), Gemini 2.5 medical scores 0.91 — beating AMIE (0.85), Mistral Med-Large (0.84), and GPT-5B-clinician (0.78). On 3D-imaging tasks (tumour segmentation, organ detection), it matches specialist models (nnU-Net 0.87 vs Gemini 0.86 Dice). Released via Google Cloud Healthcare API. HIPAA-compliant. Used in 23 NHS trusts for GP-to-specialist referral triage.</description>
        <category>CS - Medical multimodal LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Google DeepMind Health Sciences</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>o3-pro science: reasoning model solves 3 open research problems in physics + biology</title>
        <link>https://openai.com/o3-pro-science</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://openai.com/o3-pro-science</guid>
        <pubDate>Fri, 18 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>OpenAI technical report</source>
        <description>o3-pro science is OpenAI&#x27;s reasoning model fine-tuned for scientific research. It uses chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning with 10,000+ internal thinking tokens per problem, enabling it to tackle open research questions that require multi-step deductive reasoning across domains. 3 notable discoveries in 2026: (1) a novel proof that P ≠ BPP for restricted circuit classes (resolving a 30-year open problem in computational complexity), (2) a new protein-folding energy function that improves AlphaFold 3&#x27;s pLDDT by 4 percentage points on CASP17, (3) a new quantum error-correcting code for biased-noise channels (improving surface-code threshold from 1.1% to 1.7% for dephasing-biased noise). Released via OpenAI API. Each reasoning run costs ~$200 in compute (10k thinking tokens × $0.02/token). 200 research groups have used it; 12 papers submitted to peer review with o3-pro as co-author.</description>
        <category>CS - Scientific reasoning LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>OpenAI Research</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>IBM Quantum-Heron 5: 1,331-qubit modular quantum computer with 0.1% error rate</title>
        <link>https://research.ibm.com/quantum-heron-5</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://research.ibm.com/quantum-heron-5</guid>
        <pubDate>Sun, 20 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>IBM Research blog</source>
        <description>Quantum-Heron 5 is IBM&#x27;s 5th-generation superconducting quantum processor. 1,331 qubits (vs Heron 4&#x27;s 462) arranged in a modular 11×11 lattice. Two-qubit gate error rate: 0.1% (vs 0.3% in Heron 4). Achieves quantum advantage on the 3-SAT problem at 1,000 variables (classical estimate: 10^15 years). Key innovation: modular scaling via chip-to-chip coupling. 11 chips of 121 qubits each, coupled via tunable couplers with 0.05% cross-chip error. This modular approach enables scaling to 10,000+ qubits without the fabrication-yield cliff of monolithic chips. Available via IBM Quantum cloud. 200 university + 30 industry research groups have access. Used for: quantum chemistry (FeMoco simulation, 87 qubits), optimisation (portfolio optimisation, 500 variables), and cryptography (post-quantum key distribution).</description>
        <category>Physics - Modular quantum computing</category>
        <dc:creator>IBM Quantum</dc:creator>
      </item>
